  "base_commit": "5abe5b9ae77fafcb0f49dfff0211bb93b56e3aad",
  "pr_number": 5491,
  "issue_number": 5466,
  "issue_title": "fix: inferSource/presentation-lib/artifacts-lib treat the always-present self-referential githubUrl as proof of a real external source",
  "issue_body": "## Goal\nMake every call site that checks \"does this entry have an external source\" exclude the always-present, self-referential `entry.githubUrl`, the way `packages/registry/src/quality-lib.js`'s `buildSourceProvenance` already correctly does \u2014 instead of naively treating `entry.repoUrl || entry.githubUrl` as proof of a real external source.\n\n## Why this matters\n`entry.githubUrl` is not the tool's own repository \u2014 `packages/registry/src/content-builder-lib.js:414` sets it unconditionally, for every single content entry, to `buildGitHubUrl(filePath, repoRoot)`: a link to that entry's own `.mdx` file inside `github.com/JSONbored/awesome-claude` (this directory's own repo). `packages/registry/src/llms-lib.js:168` labels it explicitly as `` `Directory source: ${entry.githubUrl}` ``, distinct from `` `Repository: ${entry.repoUrl}` ``. The codebase already has one place that handles this correctly \u2014 `quality-lib.js`'s `buildSourceProvenance` explicitly filters out any URL containing `github.com/JSONbored/awesome-claude` before counting something as an `externalSourceUrl`, and treats a `githubUrl`-only entry as the lowest real tier (`\"local-editorial-source\"`), below `repo`/`docs`/`first-party`. But several other places check `entry.repoUrl || entry.githubUrl` (or equivalent) with no such filtering \u2014 since `githubUrl` is always truthy, these checks are effectively unconditional and can never distinguish \"has a real external source\" from \"has none.\"\n\n## Current behavior\n- `apps/web/src/lib/entry-normalize-lib.ts:278` (`inferSource`) \u2014 `if (entry.repoUrl || entry.githubUrl || entry.trustSignals?.sourceStatus === \"available\") return \"source-backed\";` always matches via `githubUrl`, so entries with no real repo still get classified `\"source-backed\"` instead of falling through to `\"external\"`/`\"unverified\"`.\n- `packages/registry/src/presentation-lib.js:288` \u2014 the `\"source\"` badge (`\"Source or repository link available\"`) fires for `entry.repoUrl || entry.githubUrl`, so every entry gets it.\n- `packages/registry/src/presentation-lib.js:349` (`getEntryAccessSummary`'s `hasSource`) \u2014 same unconditional `entry.repoUrl || entry.githubUrl`.\n- `packages/registry/src/artifacts-lib.js:1144` \u2014 plugin manifest `sourceUrl: entry.repoUrl || entry.githubUrl || entry.documentationUrl` will surface the self-referential directory link as a plugin's \"source\" for any entry without a real `repoUrl`.\n- Compare the correct pattern: `packages/registry/src/quality-lib.js:47-69` (`buildSourceProvenance`) filters `github.com/JSONbored/awesome-claude` out of `externalSourceUrls` before treating anything as a real external source.\n\n## Desired behavior\n`inferSource`, the two `presentation-lib.js` checks, and `artifacts-lib.js`'s plugin `sourceUrl` fallback all exclude the self-referential HeyClaude-directory URL before treating `githubUrl` as evidence of a real external source \u2014 either by reusing/extracting `buildSourceProvenance`'s filtering logic, or by applying the same `!url.includes(\"github.com/JSONbored/awesome-claude\")` guard inline. An entry with no real `repoUrl`/`documentationUrl`/`websiteUrl` should correctly fall through to `\"external\"`/`\"unverified\"` (in `inferSource`) and should not get the `\"source\"` trust badge or count as `hasSource`, purely because of its always-present directory link.\n\n## Scope\n- apps/web/src/lib/entry-normalize-lib.ts (`inferSource`)\n- packages/registry/src/presentation-lib.js (the badge check at ~line 288 and `hasSource` at ~line 349)\n- packages/registry/src/artifacts-lib.js (the plugin `sourceUrl` fallback at ~line 1144)\n\n## Out of scope\n- `quality-lib.js`'s `buildSourceProvenance` (already correct, reference implementation)\n- `llms-lib.js`'s use of `githubUrl` (already correctly labeled \"Directory source\", a legitimate distinct use)\n- `presentation-lib.js:155`'s `\"See GitHub for instructions\"` fallback line and `sourceUrlsForEntry` in `artifacts-lib.js:473-484` (both intentionally include the directory link as one of several possible source URLs to show/list, not as a boolean \"has real source\" gate \u2014 different concern, don't expand scope here)\n- Changing what `buildGitHubUrl`/`entry.githubUrl` itself contains (already correct and useful as a last-resort \"view the raw content\" link)\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- PR includes `Closes #<issue>`.\n- An entry with no `repoUrl`/`documentationUrl`/`websiteUrl` (only the always-present self-referential `githubUrl`) no longer gets classified `\"source-backed\"` by `inferSource`, no longer gets the `\"source\"` badge, and no longer counts as `hasSource`.\n- An entry with a real `repoUrl` is unaffected.\n- The plugin manifest's `sourceUrl` only uses the self-referential link as an actual last resort when there is truly no `documentationUrl` either \u2014 or note in the PR if the maintainer decides this one is an intentional exception, since a plugin manifest arguably does want *some* URL rather than none.\n\n## Quality evidence required in the PR\n- No visual impact except: some entries currently showing a \"source\" badge will stop showing it (call this out explicitly \u2014 it's a real behavior change to trust signaling that should be spot-checked against a few real entries).\n- List which real content-directory entries (spot check a few \"guide\"/\"rule\" categories with no upstream project) change classification as a result.\n\n## Validation\npnpm exec vitest run tests/entry-normalize.test.ts tests/entry-normalize-lib.test.ts tests/presentation-lib.test.ts tests/artifacts-lib.test.ts tests/registry-artifacts-lib.test.ts tests/quality-lib.test.ts\npnpm build\ngit diff --check\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-23T09:20:25.000Z",
